      "body": "## Finding Description and Impact\nWhen a user buys launchToken, slippage may occur.\n\n### Assumptions\n1.User1 bought launchTokens equivalent to 90% of the BONDING_SUPPLY from the launchpad.\n2.User2 attempts to buy launchTokens equivalent to 20% of the BONDING_SUPPLY from the launchpad. User2 uses the quoteQuoteForBase() function in SimpleBondingCurve.sol to calculate the required amount of quoteToken and sets slippage protection accordingly.\n\n### Description\nLet's examine User2's buying process:\nIn the buy() function of launchpad.sol, since 90% of the launchTokens from the BONDING_SUPPLY have already been sold, the remaining 10% is allocated to User2 using the bonding curve.\nSubsequently, because the total sold launchTokens have reached the BONDING_SUPPLY, the contract attempts to swap the remaining 10% and give it to User2.\nAlthough a slippage check is performed during the swap, if slippage occurs, the function does not revert. Instead, it treats the swap as unsuccessful and returns the tokens. This results in the loss of the intended slippage protection functionality.\n\nSee _createPairAndSwapRemaining function in launchpad.sol.\n```solidity\nfunction _createPairAndSwapRemaining(\n        address token,\n        IUniswapV2Pair pair,\n        LaunchData memory data,\n        uint256 remainingBase,\n        uint256 remainingQuote,\n        address recipient\n    ) internal returns (uint256 additionalQuoteUsed) {\n        ...\n        if (remainingBase > 0 && remainingQuote > 0) {\n            uint256 quoteNeeded =\n                uniV2Router.getAmountIn({amountOut: remainingBase, reserveIn: quoteToLock, reserveOut: tokensToLock});\n\n            if (remainingQuote >= quoteNeeded) { //<mention> : If this condition is not satisfied, slippage may occur but will not revert.\n                SwapRemainingData memory d = SwapRemainingData({\n                    token: token,\n                    quote: data.quote,\n                    recipient: recipient,\n                    baseAmount: remainingBase,\n                    quoteAmount: quoteNeeded\n                });\n\n                (, uint256 quoteUsed) = _swapRemaining(d);\n                return quoteUsed;\n            }\n        }\n\n        return 0;\n    }\n```\n### Impact\nConsequently, User2 ends up receiving only 10% of the BONDING_SUPPLY (at a higher price than initially calculated) instead of the intended 20%.\nA more critical issue is that since the sold launchToken amount has reached the BONDING_SUPPLY, _launches[buyData.token].active is set to false, User2 can't sell launchToken again.\nFinally, slippage may occur.\n\n```solidity\nfunction _graduate(...) internal returns (uint256 finalAmountOutBaseActual, uint256 finalAmountInQuote) {\n\t...\n        _launches[buyData.token].active = false;\n        ...\n    }\n```\n## Recommended Mitigation Steps\n1. The quoteQuoteForBase() function in SimpleBondingCurve.sol must accurately return the required quoteToken amount, accounting for the scenario where the requested buy exceeds the remaining BONDING_SUPPLY.\n2. In the buy() function, if the swap for the remaining launchTokens cannot be executed within the specified slippage tolerance, the transaction should revert to properly enforce slippage protection.",
      "proofOfConcept": "This issue can be demonstrated using the provided test_Slippage function.\n\nLog of test_Slippage()\n\nLogs:\n  base1 :  720000000000000000000000000\n  baseActual :  720000000000000000000000000\n  expectedQuote :  25714285714285714285\n  quoteActual :  25714285714285714285\n  expected price :  28000000\n  Actual price :  28000000\n  base2 :  160000000000000000000000000\n  baseActual :  80000000000000000000000000\n  expectedQuote :  47619047619047619046\n  quoteActual :  14285714285714285714\n  expected price :  3360000  \n  Actual price :  ***5600000*** (Actual price > expected price)\n  token.balanceOf(userA) 800000000000000000000000000\n\n\n```solidity\n// SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT\npragma solidity ^0.8.27;\n\nimport {Launchpad} from \"contracts/launchpad/Launchpad.sol\";\nimport {ILaunchpad} from \"contracts/launchpad/interfaces/ILaunchpad.sol\";\nimport {SimpleBondingCurve} from \"contracts/launchpad/BondingCurves/SimpleBondingCurve.sol\";\nimport {IBondingCurveMinimal} from \"contracts/launchpad/BondingCurves/IBondingCurveMinimal.sol\";\nimport {LaunchToken} from \"contracts/launchpad/LaunchToken.sol\";\nimport {LaunchpadLPVault} from \"contracts/launchpad/LaunchpadLPVault.sol\";\nimport {IDistributor} from \"contracts/launchpad/interfaces/IDistributor.sol\";\nimport {Distributor} from \"contracts/launchpad/Distributor.sol\";\nimport {GTELaunchpadV2PairFactory} from \"contracts/launchpad/uniswap/GTELaunchpadV2PairFactory.sol\";\nimport {GTELaunchpadV2Pair} from \"contracts/launchpad/uniswap/GTELaunchpadV2Pair.sol\";\nimport \"contracts/launchpad/libraries/RewardsTracker.sol\";\nimport {ERC20} from \"@solady/tokens/ERC20.sol\";\n\nimport {ERC1967Factory} from \"@solady/utils/ERC1967Factory.sol\";\n\nimport {ERC20Harness} from \"../harnesses/ERC20Harness.sol\";\n\nimport {MockUniV2Router} from \"../mocks/MockUniV2Router.sol\";\nimport {MockDistributor} from \"../mocks/MockDistributor.sol\";\n\nimport {FixedPointMathLib} from \"@solady/utils/FixedPointMathLib.sol\";\nimport {ICLOBManager} from \"contracts/clob/ICLOBManager.sol\";\nimport {IOperatorPanel} from \"contracts/utils/interfaces/IOperatorPanel.sol\";\n\nimport {UniV2Bytecode} from \"./integration/UniV2Bytecode.t.sol\";\n\nimport \"forge-std/Test.sol\";\n\ncontract LaunchpadTest is Test {\n    using FixedPointMathLib for uint256;\n\n    ERC1967Factory factory;\n    Launchpad launchpad;\n    GTELaunchpadV2PairFactory v2Factory;\n    Distributor distributor;\n    IBondingCurveMinimal curve;\n    LaunchpadLPVault launchpadLPVault;\n\n    ERC20Harness quoteToken;\n    MockUniV2Router uniV2Router;\n\n    address owner = makeAddr(\"owner\");\n    address user = makeAddr(\"user\");\n    address dev = makeAddr(\"dev\");\n    address user1 = makeAddr(\"user1\");\n\n    uint256 constant MIN_BASE_AMOUNT = 100_000_000;\n\n    address token;\n\n    uint256 BONDING_SUPPLY;\n    uint256 TOTAL_SUPPLY;\n\n    function setUp() public {\n        quoteToken = new ERC20Harness(\"Quote\", \"QTE\");\n\n        factory = new ERC1967Factory();\n\n        address uniV2Factory = makeAddr(\"factory\");\n        vm.etch(uniV2Factory, UniV2Bytecode.UNIV2_FACTORY);\n\n        bytes32 launchpadSalt = bytes32(abi.encode(\"GTE.V1.TESTNET.LAUNCHPAD\", owner));\n        launchpad = Launchpad(factory.predictDeterministicAddress(launchpadSalt));\n\n        address c_logic = address(new SimpleBondingCurve(address(launchpad)));\n        address v_logic = address(new LaunchpadLPVault());\n\n        curve = SimpleBondingCurve(factory.deploy(address(c_logic), owner));\n        launchpadLPVault = LaunchpadLPVault(factory.deploy(address(v_logic), owner));\n\n        address clobManager = makeAddr(\"clob manager\");\n        address operatorAddr = makeAddr(\"operator\");\n        vm.mockCall(\n            operatorAddr,\n            abi.encodeWithSelector(IOperatorPanel.getOperatorRoleApprovals.selector, user, address(0)),\n            abi.encode(0)\n        );\n\n        vm.startPrank(owner);\n        distributor = new Distributor();\n        distributor.initialize(address(launchpad));\n\n        address f_logic = address(new GTELaunchpadV2PairFactory(address(this), address(launchpad), address(launchpad), address(distributor)));\n        v2Factory = GTELaunchpadV2PairFactory(factory.deploy(address(f_logic), owner));\n        uniV2Router = new MockUniV2Router(address(v2Factory));\n        vm.stopPrank();\n        vm.label(address(distributor), \"MOCK_DISTRIBUTOR\");\n\n        address l_logic =\n            address(new Launchpad(address(uniV2Router), address(0), clobManager, operatorAddr, address(distributor)));\n\n        vm.prank(owner);\n        Launchpad(\n            factory.deployDeterministicAndCall({\n                implementation: l_logic,\n                admin: owner,\n                salt: launchpadSalt,\n                data: abi.encodeCall(\n                    Launchpad.initialize,\n                    (\n                        owner,\n                        address(quoteToken),\n                        address(curve),\n                        address(launchpadLPVault),\n                        abi.encode(200_000_000 ether, 10 ether)\n                    )\n                )\n            })\n        );\n\n        token = _launchToken();\n\n        BONDING_SUPPLY = curve.bondingSupply(token);\n        TOTAL_SUPPLY = curve.totalSupply(token);\n\n        vm.startPrank(user);\n        quoteToken.approve(address(launchpad), type(uint256).max);\n        ERC20Harness(token).approve(address(launchpad), type(uint256).max);\n        vm.stopPrank();\n    }\n\n    function _launchToken() internal returns (address) {\n        uint256 fee = launchpad.launchFee();\n        deal(dev, 30 ether);\n\n        vm.prank(dev);\n        return launchpad.launch{value: fee}(\"TestToken\", \"TST\", \"https://testtoken.com\");\n    }\n\n    function test_Slippage() public {\n        uint256 base1 = BONDING_SUPPLY / 10 * 9;\n        uint256 base2 = BONDING_SUPPLY / 10 * 2;\n        uint256 quoteTotal = curve.quoteQuoteForBase(token, BONDING_SUPPLY, true);\n\n        quoteToken.mint(user, quoteTotal*2);\n\n        //buy base1\n        uint256 expectedQuote = curve.quoteQuoteForBase(token, base1, true);\n        vm.startPrank(user);\n        (uint256 baseActual, uint256 quoteActual) = launchpad.buy(\n            ILaunchpad.BuyData({\n                account: user,\n                token: token,\n                recipient: user,\n                amountOutBase: base1,\n                maxAmountInQuote: expectedQuote\n            })\n        );\n\n        console.log(\"base1 : \", base1);\n        console.log(\"baseActual : \", baseActual);\n        console.log(\"expectedQuote : \", expectedQuote);\n        console.log(\"quoteActual : \", quoteActual);\n        console.log(\"expected price : \", baseActual/quoteActual);\n        console.log(\"Actual price : \", base1/expectedQuote);\n\n        //buy base2\n        expectedQuote = curve.quoteQuoteForBase(token, base2, true);\n        (baseActual, quoteActual) = launchpad.buy(\n            ILaunchpad.BuyData({\n                account: user,\n                token: token,\n                recipient: user,\n                amountOutBase: base2,\n                maxAmountInQuote: expectedQuote\n            })\n        );\n\n        console.log(\"base2 : \", base2);\n        console.log(\"baseActual : \", baseActual);\n        console.log(\"expectedQuote : \", expectedQuote);\n        console.log(\"quoteActual : \", quoteActual);\n        console.log(\"expected price : \", base2/expectedQuote);\n        console.log(\"Actual price : \", baseActual/quoteActual);\n\n        console.log(\"token.balanceOf(userA)\", LaunchToken(token).balanceOf(user));\n\n        vm.stopPrank();\n    }\n}\n```",
